        "text": "Magnets are used in many homes, schools and workshops in Ghana.\n\n**(a)** Name **two** magnetic materials and **two** non-magnetic materials.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(b)** State what happens when the north pole of one bar magnet is brought near the north pole of another bar magnet, and what happens when it is brought near a south pole.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(c)** State **two** differences between a permanent magnet and a temporary magnet.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(d)** Describe how you would make a steel knitting needle into a magnet by the single-touch (stroking) method.  **[3 marks]**\n\n---"
