    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) Award marks for correct points, not for repeating the question. (3) For procedures and design tasks, award method marks. (4) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed. (5) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required.)*\n\n### Question 1 (8 marks)\n\n**(a)** [2 marks]\n\n- A vector is an **organism (insect or other animal) that carries a disease-causing organism** from one host to another.\n- The vector itself may not become sick; it only carries the germ to the person or animal it bites.\n  - *Marking note: 1 mark each for any TWO correct points (2 marks). Award 1 mark for ‘an insect that carries disease’ if it is not developed further. Do NOT accept ‘an animal that causes disease’ on its own - the vector carries the germ, it does not make the germ.*\n\n**(b)** [4 marks]\n\n- **Egg**\n- **Larva** (wriggler)\n- **Pupa**\n- **Adult** (imago)\n  - *Marking note: 1 mark each for all FOUR stages in the correct order (4 marks). The order must be correct for full marks; an order that puts the pupa before the larva earns a maximum of 2 marks and a comment.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Water:** the egg, the larva and the pupa\n- **Land/air:** the adult mosquito\n  - *Marking note: 1 mark for naming the water stages and 1 mark for the adult stage (2 marks). Accept ‘the young stages (egg, larva, pupa) live in water’.*\n\n### Question 2 (9 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- (i) **eggs** (laid on the surface of water)\n- (ii) **larva** (wriggler)\n- (iii) **pupa**\n- (iv) **adult mosquito**\n  - *Marking note: 1 mark each (4 marks). The stage must be matched to the correct number. Accept ‘wriggler’ for (ii) and ‘imago’ for (iv).*\n\n**(b)** [1 marks]\n\n- **Complete metamorphosis**\n  - *Marking note: 1 mark. Do NOT accept ‘incomplete metamorphosis’ or ‘metamorphosis’ alone.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- The **larva lives in water** and has **no wings**; the **adult lives on land** and **has wings**.\n- The larva **breathes through a tube** at the water surface and feeds on tiny water plants or animals; the adult feeds on **nectar (male) or blood (female)**.\n- The larva **crawls (wriggles)** while the adult **flies**.\n  - *Marking note: 1 mark each for any TWO correct differences (2 marks). The difference must be a comparison between (ii) and (iv); a statement about only one of them earns no mark.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- The **young stages (egg, larva and pupa) can only develop in water** - they need water to live (1 mark).\n- The larva and pupa **breathe air at the surface** of the water, so the eggs must be laid where there is water (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 2 marks, 1 mark each. Accept ‘the young ones cannot live outside water’ for the first mark and ‘they need water to breathe and grow’ for the second.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- I - **proboscis**\n- II - **antenna** (antennae)\n- III - **wings**\n- IV - **abdomen**\n  - *Marking note: 1 mark each (4 marks). The label must be matched to the correct part. Do NOT accept ‘nose’ for I or ‘tail’ for IV.*\n\n**(b)** [2 marks]\n\n- The proboscis **pierces the skin** and is used for **sucking blood** (1 mark).\n- In the female Anopheles it also **passes the plasmodium (the malaria germ) into the blood** of the person she bites (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 2 marks, 1 mark each. Award the first mark for piercing/sucking; the second mark is for the link with malaria. Accept ‘it is the mouth part of the mosquito’ only with piercing or sucking.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- Only the **female bites human beings and takes blood** (1 mark).\n- She needs the blood for the **development of her eggs**, and the **plasmodium in her body is passed into the person's blood** when she bites (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 2 marks, 1 mark each. Do NOT award a mark for ‘the male has no proboscis’ - that statement is wrong.*\n\n**(d)** [1 marks]\n\n- It rests with its **body at an angle (sloping) to the surf"
